    "answer": {
      "short": "$24^\\circ$ and $36^\\circ$.",
      "worked": "The angles in a triangle sum to $180^\\circ$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Remaining angle total}&=180^\\circ-120^\\circ=60^\\circ\\\\(2+3)\\text{ parts}&=60^\\circ\\\\1\\text{ part}&=60^\\circ\\div5=12^\\circ\\\\2\\text{ parts}&=2\\times12^\\circ=24^\\circ\\\\3\\text{ parts}&=3\\times12^\\circ=36^\\circ\\end{align*}$$\nThe other angles are $24^\\circ$ and $36^\\circ$.",
